  "cover_question": "黏得不牢的胶，为什么成了畅销文具？",
  "reading_note": "超过90%说愿意购买，指试用后的受访者，不是所有消费者，也不是实际购买率。",
  "illustration_prompt": "Create a single publication-quality landscape 3:2 narrative illustration for an adult illustrated English-reading booklet. Finished standalone artwork, not a book mockup, not a collage of multiple unrelated panels. Sophisticated contemporary editorial gouache and watercolor, carefully controlled colored-pencil accents, velvety matte paint, subtle warm paper texture, soft natural daylight. Warm ivory paper dominates; subdued eucalyptus and sage greens structure the composition; restrained buttery lemon-yellow and dusty terracotta accents. Calm, comfortable, refined, credible drawing and natural anatomy. An airy coherent composition with one clear story focal point and at most two supporting details, generous breathing room at all edges and softly feathered painted edges into ivory. Detailed but uncluttered. Historically and scientifically appropriate objects, clothing and setting. Show the particular article's pivotal event or mechanism rather than a generic portrait or generic textbook symbols. Human figures treated with dignity; no grotesque caricature, no sensational violence or visible injuries. For disasters, emphasize the setting, evidence or human response without graphic suffering. For uncertain scientific claims, depict the observations and investigation without presenting debated mechanisms as proven. Absolutely no typography, captions, letters, numbers, logos, watermarks, diagram labels, fake writing or invented charts anywhere. Do not render invisible forces as literal magic. Avoid corporate vector icons, slick 3D rendering and childish cartoon style. High-quality, print-ready visual storytelling, matching a warm ivory-and-sage adult watercolor booklet.\n\nSpecific scene: The pivotal hymn-book bookmark idea, close view of an adult's two anatomically natural hands at a modest 1970s wooden reading table. One hand gently peels a small plain buttery-yellow sticky paper bookmark from an open sage clothbound hymn book while the other steadies the undamaged blank page. Two loose plain paper bookmarks rest beside the book, quietly explaining the former slipping problem. Blank book pages with faint paper texture only, absolutely no musical notation, letters, words or logos. Show the flexible note curling cleanly away without torn fibers, not strong glue strands. Airy ivory composition, tactile matte paper, elegant adult watercolor.",
